From f1375d04d005cf7489f7f74e44c4cefebe825918 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LegendaryFire <tristan.balon@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:05:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Serve Inkling 2: its tokenizer, chat template and reply
 format

The tokenizer had no rule for the inkling2 pre-tokenizer (llama.cpp's
GPT4O), the chat template's {% generation %} tag did not parse, the
reply was read as Qwen's <think>/<tool_call> markup and the end of a
turn was not a stop token. Now the tokenizer splits with the o200k
pattern, the tag renders its body, InklingOutputParser reads the
thinking / text / tool-call blocks (llama.cpp's common/parsers/
inkling.cpp), the effort words are the template's, and the GGUF's
eos / eot end a reply. The thinking budget and the forced call, which
write Qwen's markup, are off for this family.
---
